      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "description": "Nyatiti",
      "source_category": "(Wikipedia article)"
    },
    {
      "title": "African local music instrument -Nyatiti 01.jpg",
      "thumb_url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/African_local_music_instrument_-Nyatiti_01.jpg/960px-African_local_music_instrument_-Nyatiti_01.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail",
      "page_url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AAfrican%20local%20music%20instrument%20-Nyatiti%2001.jpg",
      "credit": "Onesmo Daniel",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "description": "Traditional music in most of the continent is passed down orally (or aurally) and is not written. In  African producing instruments include Nyatiti.This woman is playing Nyatiti during School Cultural day In Tanzania",
      "source_category": "nyatiti"
